#: ../../../ros_integration.md:1
msgid "ROS Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:3
msgid ""
"Most of the Ignition libraries use [Ignition Transport](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/gz-transport) to exchange data between different software "
"components. This tutorial details how to interface with [ROS](http://www.ros."
"org/), enabling the ability to use tools such as [Rviz](http://wiki.ros.org/"
"rviz) for robot or sensor visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:9
msgid ""
"**Important**: The packages documented here used to have the `ros1_` prefix "
"instead of `ros_`. Please update your code accordingly in order to avoid "
"adverse effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:13
msgid "ros_ign_bridge to the rescue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:15
msgid ""
"ros_ign_bridge provides a network bridge which enables the exchange of "
"messages between ROS 1 and Ignition Transport. Its support is limited to "
"only certain message types. Please, read this [README](https://github.com/"
"osrf/ros_ign/blob/melodic/ros_ign_bridge/README.md) to verify if your "
"message type is supported by the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:20
msgid "How to install ros_ign_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:22
msgid "Binary install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:24
msgid ""
"Citadel binaries are available for ROS Noetic and Foxy. Check out the [table "
"on ros_ign](https://github.com/ignitionrobotics/ros_ign) for other "
"combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:26
msgid "For example, to install on Noetic use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:28
msgid ""
"sudo apt install ros-noetic-ros-ign\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:33
msgid "Source install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:35
msgid ""
"See the [prerequisites](https://github.com/osrf/ros_ign/tree/melodic/"
"ros_ign_bridge#prerequisites) and [install section](https://github.com/osrf/"
"ros_ign/tree/melodic/ros_ign_bridge#building-the-bridge-from-source) of the "
"bridge documentation. This tutorial requires Ubuntu Bionic or newer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:39
msgid ""
"Assuming that you have ROS Melodic, you can install all dependencies with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:41
msgid ""
"sudo apt install ros-melodic-desktop ros-melodic-rqt-image-view libignition-"
"common3-dev libignition-transport8-dev libignition-msgs5-dev\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:45
msgid "Run the bridge and exchange images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:47
msgid ""
"In this example, we're going to generate Ignition Transport images using "
"Gazebo, that will be converted into ROS 1 images, and visualized with "
"rqt_viewer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:49
msgid "First we start a ROS 1 `roscore`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:51
msgid ""
"# Shell A:\n"
". /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash\n"
"roscore\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:57
msgid "Then we start Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:59
msgid ""
"# Shell B:\n"
"ign gazebo -r camera_sensor.sdf\n"
"# if you don't see the camera image in the Image Display and it stays grey, "
"press the orange refresh button\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:65
msgid ""
"Gazebo should be running and publishing images over the `/camera` topic. "
"Let's verify it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:68
msgid ""
"# Shell C:\n"
"ign topic -l | grep \"^/camera\"\n"
"/camera\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:74
msgid ""
"Then we start the parameter bridge with the previous topic. To run the "
"bridge:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:76
msgid ""
"# Shell D:\n"
". /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash\n"
"# If installed from source, make sure you've sourced the ros-ign packages "
"too\n"
"rosrun ros_ign_bridge parameter_bridge /camera@sensor_msgs/Image@ignition."
"msgs.Image\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:83
msgid "Now we start the ROS 1 GUI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:85
msgid ""
"# Shell E:\n"
". /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash\n"
"sudo apt-get install ros-melodic-rqt-image-view\n"
"rqt_image_view /camera\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:92
msgid ""
"You should see the current images in `rqt_image_view` which are coming from "
"Gazebo (published as Ignition Msgs over Ignition Transport)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:95
msgid ""
"The screenshot shows all the shell windows and their expected content (it "
"was taken using ROS Melodic):"
msgstr ""

